"Let $x$ be an odd integer larger than $1$. **Odd Goldbach conjecture.** Every odd number $x$ larger than $1$ can be expressed as the sum of at most three primes. This is a classical open problem in additive number theory. It is also commonly formulated, in an almost equivalent and slightly stronger form, by asserting that every odd number greater than seven is the sum of three odd primes; the paper proves the weaker bound of five primes."